               .cross("You waited until {V} slammed the door to say it.", "\"That is true. I said it because I was upset, and it came out wrong.\""),
               .cross("You texted a friend {V}'s address and said 'handle this.'", "\"I did, and it was a bad way to put it. I meant for him to talk to {V.him}, not hurt {V.him}.\""),
               .cross("The video has you saying it clearly.", "\"It does. I cannot take it back, and I am sorry.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} went to the door of {V}, a neighbor on Shiloh Road whom {D} believed had called in the anonymous tip about the dogs, and {V}'s doorbell camera recorded {D} saying, with sound, 'Snitches end up in the same hole as those dogs.'", "The defense will say {D} came to apologize and lost {D.his} temper only when {V} slammed the door, as the full video shows. The words were venting, with no weapon and no step inside."),
        closings: ("The recording is clear: 'Snitches end up in the same hole as those dogs.' {D} had texted a friend {V}'s address and 'handle this,' and was back after {PRIOR}.", "{D} came to apologize, was shut out, and said something angry on a porch, and no one was touched. The State must prove {D} meant {V} to fear for {V.his} safety."),
        timeline: [(0, "Evening: {DL} at {V}'s door; doorbell camera records it.")],
        identified: "The doorbell camera.",
        impact: "\"I sleep with my shotgun by the bed now, and I never used to lock my door. I called in a tip because I was worried about the neighborhood, and a man came to my door and told me where snitches end up. I haven't felt safe in my own house since.\"")

