               .direct("Is there bad blood?", "\"{V} spoke up for the waterman in {DL}'s crab pot case.\""),
               .direct("What was damaged at the landing?", "\"Two gill nets belonging to {V} were slashed where they hung drying. There were fourteen cuts with a straight blade, and it will cost $1,400 to replace them.\""),
               .direct("How did you identify {DL}?", "\"The landing's new camera shows a figure in white boots cutting the nets at 3:06 a.m. {DL}'s truck is the only one in the lot.\""),
               .direct("What was found on {DL}'s boat?", "\"A knife with net twine in the hinge. The twine matches the nets that were cut.\""),
               .direct("Is there history between them?", "\"{V} spoke up for the other waterman in {DL}'s crab pot case, and {DL} has been angry about it since.\""),
               .cross("Can you see the face?", "\"No. The hood is up.\""),
               .cross("Every waterman wears white boots.", "\"Every one. Only one truck was there.\""),
               .cross("You cannot see the face on the camera?", "\"No. The hood is up, and the picture is dark. What I can see is the build, the boots and the knife.\""),
               .cross("A teenager later said he cut the nets?", "\"A teenager admitted cutting the nets on a dare after walking down from the road. I do not know how that fits with the knife.\""),
                    .cross("Landing cameras sometimes fail at night, don't they?", "\"This one worked. It is new, and it recorded the nets being cut at 3:06 a.m.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} slashed the nets of someone who had taken sides against {D.him}.", "A faceless figure in boots everyone wears."),
        allocution: "\"It rained that night, and I went down to the landing to check my bilge pump. I did not cut anyone's nets, and I do not own a knife I would use for that. I'm sorry that {V} lost a season's gear. I'd ask the court to look at who else walks that dock at night.\"",
        truths: ("A knife with net twine in the hinge was in {DL}'s boat.",
                 "A teenager later admitted cutting the nets on a dare after walking down from the road."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you at the landing at 3 a.m.?", "\"It rained. I went to check my bilge pump.\""),
               .direct("Did you cut the nets?", "\"No. I didn't cut the nets, and I've never touched them.\""),
               .direct("What were you doing at the landing at 3 a.m.?", "\"It rained hard that night, and I went to check my bilge pump. I do that when it rains, and I was there about fifteen minutes.\""),
               .direct("Why was there twine on your knife?", "\"I cut twine and line every day on my own boat. The knife has net twine on it because I work with nets.\""),
               .direct("How do you feel about {V}?", "\"I was angry when {V} took the other man's side. A lot of people did. I did not hold a grudge that would make me cut a man's nets.\""),
               .direct("Where did you park at the landing?", "\"Next to the dock, where I always park. It is a gravel lot, and mine was the only truck that night.\""),
               .cross("Yours was the only truck.", "\"People walk down from the road.\""),
               .cross("{V} took {V.his} friend's side against you.", "\"Lots of people did. {V} took {V.his} friend's side, and so did half the room.\""),
               .cross("A figure in white boots with a knife.", "\"I wear white boots every day. Everyone at that landing does, and I cannot tell you who was on the camera.\""),
               .cross("A knife with net twine in the hinge was in your boat.", "\"I cut twine and line every day with that knife. It is how I work.\""),
                    .cross("You were at the landing at three in the morning.", "\"I was. I went to check my bilge pump because it rained hard, and I stayed about fifteen minutes.\"")],
        openings: ("Two gill nets belonging to {V} were slashed with fourteen cuts overnight at the landing. The new camera shows a figure in white boots with a knife at 3:06 a.m., {D}'s truck was the only one in the lot, and a knife with net twine in the hinge was in {D}'s boat.", "The defense will say {D} went to check a bilge pump in the rain and that every waterman wears white boots. The hood hides the face, and a teenager later admitted cutting the nets on a dare."),
        closings: ("One truck in the lot, one figure in white boots with a knife, and net twine in the hinge of the knife in {D}'s boat. {V} had spoken up against {D} in the earlier case over {PRIOR}.", "A hooded figure and a common pair of boots are not {D}. A teenager admitted cutting the nets, and the State must prove {D} was the person on the dock."),
        timeline: [(0, "3:06 a.m.: nets cut; 6 a.m.: {V} finds them.")],
        identified: "The landing camera and {DL}'s truck.",
        impact: "\"Nets are my whole season, and two of mine were slashed while they hung drying. I fished three weeks short while I replaced them, and the new twine cost me more than I had saved. It's hard to compete when someone is cutting your gear in the night.\"")

    static let landingGaff = followUp(
        key: "story.followup.landingGaff", category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Fight at Boat Landing Ends With Gaff Swing", "Waterman Charged After Swinging Gaff at Rival"],
        law: "awdw", threshold: 5, spec: "Assaulted {V} with a deadly weapon, a boat gaff, at the {PLACE.LANDING}, on {DATE}.", ages: 25...62, victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} and {V}, another waterman, argued on the dock at the {PLACE.LANDING} on {DATE} over who had the right to a channel. Witnesses agree {V} shoved {DL}. {DL} then swung a steel boat gaff that caught {V}'s shoulder and opened a cut that took nine stitches. {DL} says {V} came at {D.him} again.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Emergency Room Records", "A laceration to the shoulder closed with nine stitches."),
                E(.statement, 2, "Dockhand", "A dockhand says {V} had stepped back before the gaff came around.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Another Waterman", "A second witness says {V} was coming forward again when {DL} swung.")],
        witnessRole: "Marine Patrol officer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find?", "\"{V} bleeding from the shoulder, a steel gaff on the dock, and two witnesses telling different stories.\""),
               .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"That {V} shoved {D.him} and came back for more.\""),
               .direct("What was the argument about?", "\"Who had the right to a channel at the landing. {DL} and {V}, both watermen, argued on the dock.\""),
               .direct("What do the witnesses agree on?", "\"That {V} shoved {DL} first. {DL} then swung a steel boat gaff that caught {V}'s shoulder.\""),
               .direct("What was {V}'s injury?", "\"A laceration to the shoulder closed with nine stitches at the emergency room.\""),
               .direct("What did the dockhand say?", "\"That {V} had stepped back before the gaff came around. A second waterman says {V} was coming forward again when {DL} swung.\""),
               .cross("{V} pushed first.", "\"Everybody agrees on that. {V} pushed first, and nobody has said otherwise.\""),
               .cross("{V} is bigger than {DL}.", "\"By a good bit. {V} is noticeably bigger than {DL}.\""),
               .cross("The gaff hit the shoulder, not the head?", "\"It did. The cut was on the shoulder, and a swing at the head would have been more serious.\""),
               .cross("The two witnesses disagree?", "\"They do. A dockhand's phone video was found later, and I have not been asked to describe it.\""),
                    .cross("The ER treated {V}'s shoulder at once?", "\"Yes. {V} was bleeding badly and had nine stitches. The cut was deep, but it missed the bone.\"")],
        theory: ("A shove answered with a steel gaff.", "{D} defended {D.him}self against someone bigger coming at {D.him} again."),
        allocution: "\"{V} shoved me and came at me again, and the gaff was in my hand. I swung it without thinking, and I'm sorry that it caught {V.his} shoulder. We both work these waters, and I've known {V.him} a long time. I wish I had walked off the dock.\"",
        truths: ("The dockhand's phone video showed {V} backing away, hands down, when {DL} swung.",
                 "The dockhand's phone video showed {V} lunging with a fist raised as {DL} swung."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you swing the gaff?", "\"{V} shoved me and came at me again. It was in my hand.\""),
               .direct("Did you mean to hurt {V.him}?", "\"I meant to stop {V.him}.\""),
               .direct("How did the argument begin?", "\"{V} said the channel was his, and I said it was mine. He shoved me hard, and I nearly went into the water.\""),
               .direct("What did you do after the shove?", "\"I grabbed the gaff off the dock because it was nearest. {V} was coming at me again, and I was afraid he would push me in.\""),
               .direct("Where did you swing it?", "\"Low and across, toward his arm. I did not aim for his head, and I did not want to hurt him badly.\""),
               .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"I dropped the gaff and called for help. I stayed on the dock until the deputies arrived.\""),
               .cross("{V} had stepped back.", "\"Not from where I stood.\""),
               .cross("A steel gaff swung at a person.", "\"The gaff hit {V.his} shoulder, not {V.his} head.\""),
               .cross("You were not hurt.", "\"I had a sore arm where he shoved me. I was not bleeding, but I did not know that when I picked up the gaff.\""),
               .cross("You swung a steel gaff at a man's body.", "\"I did. I wanted him to stop. I did not want to hurt him badly.\""),
                    .cross("You did not call the sheriff yourself.", "\"I called for help on the radio, and a dockhand called the sheriff. I stayed until the deputies came.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} and {V}, both watermen, argued on the dock at the landing over who had the right to a channel. Witnesses agree {V} shoved {D}, and {D} then swung a steel boat gaff that caught {V}'s shoulder and opened a cut that took nine stitches.", "The defense will say {V} is bigger, shoved {D} first, and was coming at {D} again, and {D} swung the gaff to stop {V.him} from pushing {D.him} off the dock. {D} aimed low and stayed to call for help."),
        closings: ("A shove can be answered with words or a walk away. {D} picked up a steel gaff and swung it at a man who had already stepped back, and after {PRIOR} {D} knew what a gaff does.", "{V} shoved first, is far bigger than {D}, and came forward again. A man who swings at a shoulder to stop an attacker acts in defense, and the State must prove otherwise."),
        timeline: [(0, "Afternoon: argument on the dock; gaff swung; {V} taken for stitches.")],
        identified: "At the scene.",
        impact: "I can't lift a pot over my head yet. That's my living. The gaff opened my shoulder and took nine stitches, and the doctor says I'm weeks away from heavy work. I watch other boats go out from the landing. Every day I lose is a day of pay I can't make up.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "selfDefense"])

    // MARK: - After the motel overdose

    static let naloxoneNight = followUp(
        key: "story.followup.naloxoneNight", category: .drugs,
        headlines: ["Friend Revived With Naloxone After Pills From Same Supplier", "Second Overdose Tied to Defendant in Motel Death Case"],
        law: "deliverSchedII", threshold: 6, spec: "Delivered fentanyl, a Schedule II controlled substance, to {V}, on {DATE}.", ages: 19...35, victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {V} stopped breathing in a car outside a convenience store on {DATE} and was revived by a deputy with two doses of naloxone. {V} told the deputy {D} had given {V.him} a blue pill twenty minutes earlier. Texts on {V}'s phone show {V} asking {DL} for \"one\" and {DL} answering \"outside.\"",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Texts", "\"u got one?\" / \"outside\" from {DL}'s number, twenty minutes before the 911 call."),
                E(.forensic, 2, "Lab Report", "A second pill in {V}'s pocket contained fentanyl.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Recanted", "{V} later told the defense {V.he} doesn't remember who gave {V.him} the pill.")],
        witnessRole: "Narcotics detective",
        exam: [.direct("What do the texts show?", "\"{V} asks for one, and {DL} answers 'outside.' Twenty minutes later {V} isn't breathing.\""),
               .direct("What did {V} say at the scene?", "\"That {DL} gave {V.him} the pill. The deputy's camera recorded it.\""),
               .direct("What happened outside the convenience store?", "\"{V} stopped breathing in a car. A deputy revived {V.him} with two doses of naloxone, and {V} was taken to the hospital.\""),
               .direct("What did the lab find?", "\"A second pill in {V}'s pocket contained fentanyl.\""),
               .direct("What happened when the deputy arrived?", "\"He found {V} slumped in the driver's seat, gave naloxone twice, and {V} came around coughing.\""), .direct("What did the deputy find on {V}?", "\"A second pill in {V}'s pocket. The lab confirmed it contained fentanyl.\""),
                    .cross("{V} says now {V.he} doesn't remember.", "\"{V} said it clearly at the scene, on camera.\""),
               .cross("No money changed hands?", "\"Delivery doesn't require money. A delivery can happen without anyone paying.\""),
               .cross("{V} told the defense {V.he} does not remember?", "\"Later, yes. At the scene {V} was clear on the camera, though barely awake.\""),
               .cross("Another car pulled alongside {V}'s?", "\"The store's camera shows a different car pulled alongside, and that driver was later charged. {DL}'s car was also on the camera, parked beside {V}'s at the time of the text.\""),
                    .cross("{V} named {DL} at the scene on camera.", "\"{V} did, in a slurred voice, as the deputy was working on {V.him}. The camera recorded it.\"")],
        theory: ("After {V}'s friend died, {D} handed out fentanyl again, and another friend nearly died.", "{V} doesn't remember who gave {V.him} the pill."),
        allocution: "\"I did not give {V} a blue pill or go meet {V.him} that night. I texted back, but I never went. I'm heartbroken that {V} stopped breathing, and I'm grateful the deputy was there. I'd ask the court to look at who really handed {V.him} that pill.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s car was on the store's camera, parked beside {V}'s, at the time of the text.",
                 "The store's camera showed a different car pull alongside {V}'s, and the driver was later charged."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you give {V} a pill?", "\"No. I texted back but I never went.\""),
               .direct("Why say 'outside'?", "\"I was going to, and I didn't.\""),
               .direct("What happened that night?", "\"{V} texted me and asked if I had one. I texted back 'outside,' and I meant to go, and I did not.\""),
               .direct("Why did you write 'outside'?", "\"I was going to bring one. Then I thought about my friend who died, and I stopped before I left the house.\""),
               .direct("Where were you at that time?", "\"In my car down the block. My car was on the camera, parked beside {V}'s because I pulled in to talk to {V.him} and left.\""),
               .direct("Did you hand {V} a pill?", "\"No. I never gave {V} a pill. I did not touch {V}'s car.\""),
               .cross("{V} named you on the deputy's camera.", "\"{V.He} was barely awake. When {V} named me on the deputy's camera, {V.he} could hardly keep {V.his} eyes open.\""),
               .cross("After what happened in Room 112.", "\"I know. That's why I didn't go.\""),
               .cross("You said 'outside' twenty minutes before the 911 call.", "\"I did, and I did not go. Another car came up while I was still sitting there.\""),
               .cross("Your car was beside {V}'s when you texted.", "\"It was. I pulled in because I was going to talk to {V.him}, and I did not give {V.him} anything.\""),
                    .cross("You told {V} 'outside' and then stayed in your car.", "\"I did. I sat there and thought about what happened the last time, and I did not go to {V}'s car.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} stopped breathing in a car outside a convenience store and was revived by a deputy with two doses of naloxone. {V} told the deputy {D} had given {V.him} a blue pill twenty minutes earlier, and texts show {V} asking {D} for one and {D} answering 'outside.'", "The defense will say {D} never delivered anything, and that a different car pulled alongside {V}'s and its driver was later charged. {V} later said {V.he} does not remember who gave {V.him} the pill."),
        closings: ("A text asking for one, an answer of 'outside,' a pill, and a deputy's camera on which {V} names {D}. A second pill in {V}'s pocket held fentanyl, and {D} was back after {PRIOR}.", "{V} was barely awake on that camera and later said {V.he} does not remember who gave {V.him} the pill. The State must prove {D} delivered it and not that another driver did."),
        timeline: [(0, "Text: \"outside.\""), (0, "Twenty minutes later: 911 call; naloxone; {V} revived.")],
        identified: "{V}'s words on the deputy's camera and the texts.",
        impact: "\"The deputy told me I was dead for two minutes before the naloxone brought me back. I have a little girl at home who almost lost her mother that night. I trusted the person who gave me that pill, and I will carry that for the rest of my life.\"")

    static let fentanylCrash = followUp(
        key: "story.followup.fentanylCrash", category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Driver Nodding Off on Fentanyl Crashes Into Mailboxes", "DWI Charge After Driver Found Slumped at Wheel"],
        law: "dwi", threshold: 5, spec: "Drove a vehicle on {STREET} while under the influence of an impairing substance, fentanyl, on {DATE}.", ages: 19...35, victim: false,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D}'s car left {STREET} on {DATE}, took out three mailboxes, and stopped in a yard. A deputy found {DL} slumped at the wheel with pinpoint pupils; {DL} came around after naloxone. A blood test showed fentanyl. {DL} says {D.he} swerved for a deer and hit {D.his} head.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Blood Test", "Fentanyl and norfentanyl in {DL}'s blood drawn an hour after the crash."),
                E(.video, 2, "Body Camera", "{D} slumped, pinpoint pupils, unresponsive until naloxone.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Deer", "{DL} says a deer ran out and {D.he} struck {D.his} head on the window.")],
        witnessRole: "Patrol deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find?", "\"{DL} slumped over the wheel, breathing slow, pupils like pinpoints. One dose of naloxone and {D.he} sat up.\""),
               .direct("Why does naloxone matter?", "\"It reverses opioids. It does nothing for a head injury.\""),
               .direct("How did the crash happen?", "\"{DL}'s car left {STREET}, took out three mailboxes, and stopped in a yard. No other cars were involved.\""), .direct("What condition was {DL} in?", "\"Slumped at the wheel with pinpoint pupils and unresponsive. After one dose of naloxone {D.he} came around and sat up.\""), .direct("What did the blood test show?", "\"Fentanyl and norfentanyl in {DL}'s blood, drawn an hour after the crash. A pill bottle with fentanyl residue was under the driver's seat.\""), .direct("What did the ER find?", "\"A concussion consistent with a strike to the window. That was a small bump and did not explain the pupils.\""),
                    .cross("Did you look for deer tracks?", "\"No. I didn't look for deer tracks, because I assumed I knew where the deer had been.\""),
               .cross("{DL} had a bump on the head.", "\"A small one. It was only a small bump on the head, and it wasn't bleeding.\""),
                    .cross("{DL} says a deer ran out?", "\"That is what {D.he} says. I did not find any deer hair or blood, and I looked.\""), .cross("A head injury can cause confusion, can't it?", "\"It can, but it does not make pupils pinpoint, and it does not respond to naloxone. {DL} responded to naloxone.\""), .cross("{DL} was alone in the car?", "\"Yes. No one else was hurt, and nothing else was hit besides the mailboxes.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove on fentanyl and nearly killed {D.him}self and whoever was in those yards.", "A deer and a head injury."),
        allocution: "\"A deer ran out in front of me, and I swerved and hit my head on the wheel. I don't remember much after that. I'm sorry for the three mailboxes and the fright to the family whose yard I ended up in. I know the blood test showed fentanyl, and I'm going to get help.\"",
        truths: ("A pill bottle with fentanyl residue was under the driver's seat.", "The ER found a concussion consistent with the window strike."),
        defendant: [.direct("What happened?", "\"A deer ran out. I swerved and hit my head.\""),
               .direct("The fentanyl?", "\"The fentanyl in my system was from days before, not from that night.\""),
               .direct("What do you remember about the crash?", "\"A deer ran out in front of me. I swerved and hit my head on the window, and then I do not remember much.\""),
               .direct("Why was there fentanyl in your blood?", "\"I took something days before, and I thought it was out of my system. I did not take anything that night.\""),
               .direct("What about the bottle under your seat?", "\"It was there from the days before, and I forgot it. I should have thrown it out.\""),
               .direct("How do you feel about what happened?", "\"I am lucky no one was in those yards. I am ashamed, and I am trying to stay clean.\""),
               .cross("Naloxone woke you up.", "\"I was dazed. The naloxone woke me up, but I don't remember much right after.\""),
               .cross("After your friend died from the same drug.", "\"I know. My friend died from the same drug, and I should have known better.\""),
               .cross("The deputy found no deer.", "\"I do not know where it went. It ran off, and I did not stop to look.\""),
                    .cross("The ER found fentanyl and norfentanyl in your blood.", "\"They did. I took something days before, and I did not think it would still be there.\""), .cross("A pill bottle with fentanyl residue was under your seat.", "\"It was an old bottle that I forgot. I should have thrown it out.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}'s car left {STREET}, took out three mailboxes, and stopped in a yard, with {D} slumped at the wheel, pinpoint pupils, unresponsive until naloxone. A blood test an hour later showed fentanyl, and a pill bottle with fentanyl residue was under the seat.", "The defense will say a deer ran out, {D} swerved and struck {D.his} head on the window, and the ER found a concussion. Any fentanyl was in {D}'s system from days before, not from that night."),
        closings: ("Pinpoint pupils, an unresponsive driver revived by naloxone, fentanyl in the blood an hour later, and a bottle with residue under the seat. {D} was back after {PRIOR}.", "A deer, a swerve and a concussion explain the crash, and no deer hair or blood proves nothing either way. The State must prove {D} was impaired by fentanyl at the time of the crash."),
        timeline: [(0, "Crash on {STREET}; naloxone; blood drawn an hour later.")],
        identified: "At the scene.")

